  "article": {
    "hero": {
      "title": "💅 Nail Salon Name Generator",
      "tagline": "Names for a nail salon, nail bar or home nail studio."
    },
    "intro": "A good nail salon name is short, fun and looks good on Instagram, whether you run a nail bar, a home studio or a mobile service. The **Nail Salon Name Generator** suggests names for a nail salon, nail bar, mobile nail tech or press-on brand. Pick catchy and witty, cute, modern, luxury or aesthetic, or make a nail business name with your name or your town.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Eight good nail salon names",
        "content": "<p>All eight came from the generator:</p><ul><li><strong>Gel & Gloss</strong>: two nail words that sound good together.</li><li><strong>The Final Coat</strong>: a witty name from the last step of a manicure.</li><li><strong>Buff & Shine</strong>: does exactly what it says.</li><li><strong>Bubblegum Nail Studio</strong>: cute and colourful.</li><li><strong>Lacquer</strong>: one sleek word for a modern nail bar.</li><li><strong>The Digit Room</strong>: modern and a little witty.</li><li><strong>Maison Vernis</strong>: luxury French: <em>vernis</em> means varnish, the French word for nail polish.</li><li><strong>Hampton Pedicure Bar</strong>: your town plus a speciality.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "How nail salon names work",
        "content": "<ul><li><strong>Nail words are made for names:</strong> gel, gloss, polish, lacquer, tips, buff, file and coat. Manicure comes from the Latin <em>manus</em> (hand) and pedicure from <em>pes</em> (foot).</li><li><strong>\"Nail bar\"</strong> suggests walk-in, quick appointments; <em>studio</em> and <em>atelier</em> suggest booked, detailed nail art.</li><li><strong>Mobile techs and press-on brands</strong> often use their own name, because clients follow the artist.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Check it's free before you print the sign",
        "content": "<p>A name from a generator is a starting point, not permission to use it. Before you order the sign, the boxes or the van livery:</p><ul><li><strong>Company register.</strong> In the UK, search Companies House; you can't register a limited company with the same name as an existing one. In the US, search your state's business register.</li><li><strong>Trade marks.</strong> Search the UK trade mark register (or the USPTO in the US) for the goods and services you'll sell.</li><li><strong>Domain and handles.</strong> Check the .co.uk or .com and the Instagram and TikTok handles you'll need.</li><li><strong>Your area.</strong> Search a map app for businesses with the same or a similar name nearby.</li></ul><p>Press <strong>Check</strong> on any name, or use the <a href=\"../business-name-checker.html\">Business Name Checker</a>, to run most of these at once. For the full process, read our guide, <a href=\"../guides/business-naming-best-practices.html\">Business Naming Best Practices</a>. This is general guidance, not legal advice.</p>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Making the name work",
        "content": "<ul><li><strong>Check the handle.</strong> Nail art sells on Instagram and TikTok, so the handle matters as much as the sign.</li><li><strong>Leave room for toes.</strong> If you'll offer pedicures, a name that only mentions hands can feel limiting.</li></ul><p>Offering more treatments? Try the <a href=\"beauty-salon-name-generator.html\">Beauty Salon</a>, <a href=\"lash-business-name-generator.html\">Lash Business</a> and <a href=\"hair-salon-name-generator.html\">Hair Salon</a> name generators.</p><p>For more, see all the <a href=\"../categories/biz_beauty-names.html\">beauty and wellness business name generators</a>.</p>"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": [
      {
        "question": "What are good nail salon names?",
        "answer": "Short, fun names that look good on Instagram: witty ones like The Final Coat, cute ones like Bubblegum Nail Studio, or luxury names like Maison Vernis, French for nail varnish."
      },
      {
        "question": "How do I check a nail salon name is free?",
        "answer": "Press Check on any name to see whether it's free as a company, a domain and a social media handle. In the UK, also search Companies House; in the US, search your state's business register and the USPTO trade mark search. Check your local area too, as another salon nearby with a similar name can confuse clients."
      },
      {
        "question": "Should I name my nail business after myself?",
        "answer": "It works well if you're a nail tech building a personal following: \"Nails by Sarah\" tells clients exactly who they'll see. If you plan to take on staff, open a second salon or sell one day, a name that isn't tied to you, such as \"Tips & Toes\", is easier to grow and pass on."
      },
      {
        "question": "What's the difference between a nail bar and a nail studio?",
        "answer": "A nail bar usually suggests quick, walk-in appointments; a studio suggests booked appointments and more detailed nail art. Pick the word that matches how you work."
      }
    ]
  }
